# The other killer mechanic: Creative Duolingo leagues

You could have:

```text
Bronze
Silver
Gold
Platinum
Freak
```

You earn weekly points through **actual creative performance**, not grinding XP.

Top few promote.

Bottom few demote.

But importantly, you don't need to participate every day. Maybe best 5 results of 7 count so missing Tuesday doesn't destroy your season.

---

# Each day automatically creates a mini episode

This is where your existing show technology becomes ridiculously useful.

Once the submissions are locked:

```text
ENTRIES
  ↓
Freak Town arranges them
  ↓
walkouts
  ↓
30-second performances
  ↓
Ella intros/reactions
  ↓
score reveal
  ↓
winner
```

So your six-person group receives:

> **KAMPOT LEAGUE — EPISODE 17**
> 4:32

Tap and watch the whole thing like a tiny television episode.

You can watch individually during the voting period, but afterward the **canonical episode** becomes an artifact in the group's history.

After a year:

> 218 episodes
> 1,104 performances
> 36 characters
> 12 seasons

That is genuinely cool.

