## And then you can merge this with Daily Freak puzzles

The daily competition doesn't even need to be comedy every time.

Your league receives:

> **TODAY: GET PAST TREVOR**

Everyone has six attempts.

At reveal time you watch everyone's winning route as little scenes.

Tomorrow:

> **TODAY: SURVIVE THE TSUNAMI**

Tomorrow:

> **TODAY: 30-SECOND STANDUP**

Tomorrow:

> **TODAY: MAKE THE MONK ANGRY**

So a **Freak League** is really:

> a small persistent group competing on one creative challenge each day.

Stand-up is just one event.

That might be the cleanest definition yet.

And I think the most compelling notification in the whole app could simply be:

> **Today's Freak is live.**
> Sam chose the challenge.
> You have 6 hours.

That gives Freak Town a daily heartbeat without needing everyone online simultaneously.
